{"id": "CVE-2026-10848", "identity": {"title": "CVE-2026-10848", "published": "2026-08-02 16:12:18", "modified": "2026-08-02 17:16:58", "description": "The OCPP 1.6 client in subsys/net/lib/ocpp parsed inbound WAMP RPC frames in parse_rpc_msg() (subsys/net/lib/ocpp/ocpp_j.c) using a hand-rolled helper, extract_string_field(), that copied the message's uid and action fields with strncpy(out_buf, token + 1, outlen - 1) and then scanned the result with strchr(out_buf, '\"'). Because strncpy does not NUL-terminate the destination when the source is at least outlen - 1 (127) bytes long, the subsequent strchr reads past the 128-byte destination buffer into adjacent stack memory; if a \" byte is found beyond the buffer, a one-byte out-of-bounds NUL write also occurs. A related defect in extract_payload() runs strchr/strrchr over the receive buffer, which may not be NUL-terminated when a maximal-length frame fills it.\n\nThe parsed bytes come directly from the OCPP central-system server over a websocket: the reader thread fills recv_buf via websocket_recv_msg() and calls parse_rpc_msg() on each inbound DATA frame (subsys/net/lib/ocpp/ocpp.c). A malicious or compromised central server, or an on-path attacker (OCPP is commonly deployed over plain ws://), can send an RPC frame whose uid or action field is 127+ bytes with no closing quote, triggering the out-of-bounds access.\n\nThe primary impact is a remotely triggerable denial of service: the unbounded scan can fault on an unmapped page, and the stray NUL write can corrupt adjacent stack state. The over-read data is not reflected to the peer, so disclosure is limited. The feature is EXPERIMENTAL and must be explicitly enabled (CONFIG_OCPP). The fix replaces the manual parser with the bounds-respecting json_mixed_arr_parse() and copies the extracted uid with an explicitly NUL-terminated buffer, eliminating both over-reads."}, "cvss": {"base_score": 7.0, "severity": "HIGH", "attack_vector": null, "attack_complexity": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "scope": null, "confidentiality_impact": null, "integrity_impact": null, "availability_impact": null, "band": "High"}, "epss": {"score": null, "percentile": null, "date": null}, "exploitation": {"wild_exploited": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa_kev": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa": false, "has_exploit_bulletin": false, "has_exploit_reference": true, "has_public_exploit_provider": false, "has_github_exploit": false, "top_reference_url": "https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/commit/e500f7b81b5b8a867e28b2f4e59512cbfdd5ae75"}, "ssvc": {"exploitation": null, "automatable": null, "technical_impact": null, "poc": false}, "barriers": {"attack_vector": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "summary": "Unknown"}, "weakness": {"cwe_ids": ["CWE-125", "CWE-787"], "cwe_primary": "CWE-125", "cwe_family": null, "cwe_names": {"CWE-125": "Out-of-bounds Read", "CWE-787": "Out-of-bounds Write"}}, "software": {"vendors": "zephyrproject", "products": "zephyr", "cpe_uris": null, "software_map": [{"key": "zephyrproject:zephyr", "vendor": "zephyrproject", "product": "zephyr", "source": "cpe", "sample_cpe": "cpe:2.3:o:zephyrproject:zephyr:*:-:*:*:*:*:*:*", "category": null, "platform": null, "surface": null, "tags": null}]}, "references": ["https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/commit/e500f7b81b5b8a867e28b2f4e59512cbfdd5ae75", "https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/security/advisories/GHSA-jgqq-7mjj-w642"], "sources": {"vulners_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-10848", "nvd_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-10848"}}
{"id": "CVE-2026-9856", "identity": {"title": "CVE-2026-9856", "published": "2026-08-02 15:10:53", "modified": "2026-08-02 16:16:25", "description": "A vulnerability in huggingface/transformers versions <=5.8.0.dev0 allows an attacker to perform arbitrary file writes via path traversal. The issue resides in the `save_pretrained()` methods of `PreTrainedTokenizerBase` and `ProcessorMixin`, where keys from the `chat_template` dictionary are used directly as filenames without proper validation. An attacker can exploit this by publishing a malicious Hugging Face Hub repository with a crafted `tokenizer_config.json` file. When a victim downloads and saves the tokenizer or processor, the attacker-controlled keys can escape the intended save directory, enabling arbitrary file writes with attacker-controlled content. This vulnerability affects multiple processors inheriting from `ProcessorMixin`, including Idefics, Florence, Gemma, Phi, and Qwen-VL."}, "cvss": {"base_score": 7.1, "severity": "HIGH", "attack_vector": "NETWORK", "attack_complexity": "LOW", "privileges_required": "NONE", "user_interaction": "REQUIRED", "scope": "UNCHANGED", "confidentiality_impact": "NONE", "integrity_impact": "HIGH", "availability_impact": "LOW", "band": "High"}, "epss": {"score": null, "percentile": null, "date": null}, "exploitation": {"wild_exploited": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa_kev": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa": false, "has_exploit_bulletin": false, "has_exploit_reference": true, "has_public_exploit_provider": false, "has_github_exploit": false, "top_reference_url": "https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/commit/eaaaf8494dd5386634ae37d1d122212fdc315be5"}, "ssvc": {"exploitation": null, "automatable": null, "technical_impact": null, "poc": false}, "barriers": {"attack_vector": "NETWORK", "privileges_required": "NONE", "user_interaction": "REQUIRED", "summary": "network, privileges: NONE, user interaction: REQUIRED"}, "weakness": {"cwe_ids": ["CWE-22"], "cwe_primary": "CWE-22", "cwe_family": "Path Traversal", "cwe_names": {"CWE-22": "Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')"}}, "software": {"vendors": "huggingface", "products": "huggingface/transformers", "cpe_uris": "cpe:2.3:*:huggingface:huggingface\\/transformers:5.10.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*", "software_map": [{"key": "huggingface:huggingface/transformers", "vendor": "huggingface", "product": "huggingface/transformers", "source": "cna_vendor_product", "sample_cpe": null, "category": null, "platform": null, "surface": null, "tags": null}]}, "references": ["https://huntr.com/bounties/362824d5-fe18-40e8-a6cf-62277f97a170", "https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/commit/eaaaf8494dd5386634ae37d1d122212fdc315be5"], "sources": {"vulners_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-9856", "nvd_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-9856"}}
{"id": "CVE-2026-65321", "identity": {"title": "CVE-2026-65321", "published": "2026-08-02 14:56:28", "modified": "2026-08-02 15:16:33", "description": "PyAthena prior to 3.35.4 contains a sql injection vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to inject arbitrary SQL by exploiting improper quote-escaping in DefaultParameterFormatter.format(), which routes DELETE and CTAS statements to the _escape_hive function that backslash-escapes single quotes rather than doubling them. Because Athena and Trino do not treat backslashes as escape characters inside string literals, attacker-supplied input such as a single quote followed by SQL syntax causes the parser to terminate the string literal prematurely, enabling data exfiltration via UNION SELECT, execution of destructive statements, and attacker-controlled CTAS destination and content."}, "cvss": {"base_score": 9.8, "severity": "CRITICAL", "attack_vector": null, "attack_complexity": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "scope": null, "confidentiality_impact": null, "integrity_impact": null, "availability_impact": null, "band": "Critical"}, "epss": {"score": null, "percentile": null, "date": null}, "exploitation": {"wild_exploited": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa_kev": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa": false, "has_exploit_bulletin": false, "has_exploit_reference": true, "has_public_exploit_provider": false, "has_github_exploit": false, "top_reference_url": "https://github.com/laughingman7743/PyAthena/security/advisories/GHSA-xwj5-g6cv-4r5c"}, "ssvc": {"exploitation": null, "automatable": null, "technical_impact": null, "poc": false}, "barriers": {"attack_vector": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "summary": "Unknown"}, "weakness": {"cwe_ids": ["CWE-89"], "cwe_primary": "CWE-89", "cwe_family": "Injection", "cwe_names": {"CWE-89": "Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')"}}, "software": {"vendors": "laughingman7743", "products": "PyAthena", "cpe_uris": "cpe:2.3:a:laughingman7743:pyathena:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*", "software_map": []}, "references": ["https://github.com/laughingman7743/PyAthena/security/advisories/GHSA-xwj5-g6cv-4r5c", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/pyathena-sql-injection-via-defaultparameterformatter-delete-ctas", "https://github.com/laughingman7743/PyAthena", "https://github.com/pyathena-dev/PyAthena/commit/27901d12245ea722b3b4e211c60e2ade4e7c8efd"], "sources": {"vulners_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-65321", "nvd_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-65321"}}
{"id": "CVE-2026-68582", "identity": {"title": "CVE-2026-68582", "published": "2026-08-02 12:15:28", "modified": "2026-08-02 13:16:54", "description": "Vikunja versions >= 0.24.0 and <= 2.3.0 contain a broken object level authorization (BOLA) vulnerability in the task-collection endpoint (GET /api/v1/projects/{project}/views/{view}/tasks). The endpoint loads the requested project view from the URL path without verifying the caller is authorized for it. For a link-share token holder, the task scope is pinned to the share's own project, but the view is taken from the attacker-controlled path and never re-validated. As a result, a holder of any project share link can read any other tenant's kanban bucket records — bucket titles and the full created_by user object (username, name, id) — for every view in the instance. The same missing pre-authorization view load also creates a project/view-ID existence oracle (404 vs. non-404) usable by link shares and ordinary authenticated users. Task contents remain constrained to the share's own project and are not disclosed. Fixed in 2.4.0."}, "cvss": {"base_score": 9.3, "severity": "CRITICAL", "attack_vector": null, "attack_complexity": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "scope": null, "confidentiality_impact": null, "integrity_impact": null, "availability_impact": null, "band": "Critical"}, "epss": {"score": null, "percentile": null, "date": null}, "exploitation": {"wild_exploited": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa_kev": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa": false, "has_exploit_bulletin": false, "has_exploit_reference": true, "has_public_exploit_provider": false, "has_github_exploit": false, "top_reference_url": "https://github.com/go-vikunja/vikunja/security/advisories/GHSA-rj9j-8772-4h6c"}, "ssvc": {"exploitation": null, "automatable": null, "technical_impact": null, "poc": false}, "barriers": {"attack_vector": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "summary": "Unknown"}, "weakness": {"cwe_ids": ["CWE-639"], "cwe_primary": "CWE-639", "cwe_family": null, "cwe_names": {"CWE-639": "Authorization Bypass Through User-Controlled Key"}}, "software": {"vendors": "go-vikunja", "products": "vikunja", "cpe_uris": "cpe:2.3:a:go-vikunja:vikunja:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*", "software_map": []}, "references": ["https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vikunja-broken-object-level-authorization-via-link-share-token", "https://github.com/go-vikunja/vikunja/security/advisories/GHSA-rj9j-8772-4h6c"], "sources": {"vulners_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-68582", "nvd_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-68582"}}
{"id": "CVE-2026-68580", "identity": {"title": "CVE-2026-68580", "published": "2026-08-02 12:15:27", "modified": "2026-08-02 13:16:53", "description": "FreeRDP before 3.29.0 contains integer overflow vulnerabilities in the audio input redirection channel (audin) across ALSA, sndio, WinMM, and OpenSL ES backends that fail to validate the FramesPerPacket parameter from RDP servers. Attackers can supply a malicious FramesPerPacket value causing allocation size wraparound, resulting in heap-based buffer overflow on ALSA or denial of service on all platforms."}, "cvss": {"base_score": 7.7, "severity": "HIGH", "attack_vector": null, "attack_complexity": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "scope": null, "confidentiality_impact": null, "integrity_impact": null, "availability_impact": null, "band": "High"}, "epss": {"score": null, "percentile": null, "date": null}, "exploitation": {"wild_exploited": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa_kev": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa": false, "has_exploit_bulletin": false, "has_exploit_reference": true, "has_public_exploit_provider": false, "has_github_exploit": false, "top_reference_url": "https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-69xf-pqrw-596x"}, "ssvc": {"exploitation": null, "automatable": null, "technical_impact": null, "poc": false}, "barriers": {"attack_vector": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "summary": "Unknown"}, "weakness": {"cwe_ids": ["CWE-122"], "cwe_primary": "CWE-122", "cwe_family": null, "cwe_names": {"CWE-122": "Heap-based Buffer Overflow"}}, "software": {"vendors": "FreeRDP", "products": "FreeRDP", "cpe_uris": "cpe:2.3:a:freerdp:freerdp:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*", "software_map": [{"key": "freerdp:freerdp", "vendor": "FreeRDP", "product": "FreeRDP", "source": "cna_vendor_product", "sample_cpe": null, "category": null, "platform": null, "surface": null, "tags": null}]}, "references": ["https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-before-integer-overflow-via-audio-input-channel", "https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-69xf-pqrw-596x"], "sources": {"vulners_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-68580", "nvd_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-68580"}}
{"id": "CVE-2026-68581", "identity": {"title": "CVE-2026-68581", "published": "2026-08-02 12:15:27", "modified": "2026-08-02 13:16:54", "description": "Vikunja versions 0.22.0 through 2.3.0 fail to validate the principal type in API token management. Because user IDs and link-share IDs are independent numeric sequences and both resolve through a generic web.Auth.GetID() interface, a link-share JWT whose numeric ID equals a target user's ID is treated as that user by the /api/v1/tokens endpoints. An authenticated attacker can obtain a target's numeric user ID via authenticated user search, then create link shares on an attacker-writable project until the link-share sequence reaches that value, and use the resulting link-share JWT to list, create, and delete the target user's API tokens (including issuing a new token with attacker-chosen scopes under the target's permissions). Fixed in version 2.4.0."}, "cvss": {"base_score": 8.6, "severity": "HIGH", "attack_vector": null, "attack_complexity": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "scope": null, "confidentiality_impact": null, "integrity_impact": null, "availability_impact": null, "band": "High"}, "epss": {"score": null, "percentile": null, "date": null}, "exploitation": {"wild_exploited": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa_kev": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa": false, "has_exploit_bulletin": false, "has_exploit_reference": true, "has_public_exploit_provider": false, "has_github_exploit": false, "top_reference_url": "https://github.com/go-vikunja/vikunja/commit/e6b25bd57b537ef9a72b5acdadf446ca5ef77bfa"}, "ssvc": {"exploitation": null, "automatable": null, "technical_impact": null, "poc": false}, "barriers": {"attack_vector": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "summary": "Unknown"}, "weakness": {"cwe_ids": ["CWE-863"], "cwe_primary": "CWE-863", "cwe_family": null, "cwe_names": {"CWE-863": "Incorrect Authorization"}}, "software": {"vendors": "go-vikunja", "products": "vikunja", "cpe_uris": "cpe:2.3:a:go-vikunja:vikunja:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*", "software_map": []}, "references": ["https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vikunja-through-authentication-bypass-via-principal-id-collision", "https://github.com/go-vikunja/vikunja/commit/e6b25bd57b537ef9a72b5acdadf446ca5ef77bfa", "https://github.com/go-vikunja/vikunja/security/advisories/GHSA-vvcv-vpph-h844", "https://github.com/go-vikunja/vikunja/commit/95b7e673fb5ee407498fa4b13e8b4c57847a4a0b"], "sources": {"vulners_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-68581", "nvd_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-68581"}}
{"id": "CVE-2026-68579", "identity": {"title": "CVE-2026-68579", "published": "2026-08-02 12:15:26", "modified": "2026-08-02 13:16:53", "description": "FreeRDP before 3.30.0 (<= 3.29.0) contains a heap-based buffer overflow in the Windows clipboard client's CliprdrStream_Read function (client/Windows/wf_cliprdr.c). When an OLE paste consumer (e.g. explorer.exe) calls IStream::Read with a fixed-size buffer of cb bytes, CliprdrStream_Read requests file contents from the RDP server and then copies the response into the caller's buffer using the server-supplied length (req_fsize) instead of cb. A malicious or compromised RDP server can return an oversized CB_FILECONTENTS_RESPONSE, causing an out-of-bounds write of attacker-controlled data into the paste consumer's heap buffer when a user pastes server-offered clipboard file contents."}, "cvss": {"base_score": 9.6, "severity": "CRITICAL", "attack_vector": null, "attack_complexity": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "scope": null, "confidentiality_impact": null, "integrity_impact": null, "availability_impact": null, "band": "Critical"}, "epss": {"score": null, "percentile": null, "date": null}, "exploitation": {"wild_exploited": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa_kev": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa": false, "has_exploit_bulletin": false, "has_exploit_reference": true, "has_public_exploit_provider": false, "has_github_exploit": false, "top_reference_url": "https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/commit/5e8e987b469b60a3bafadf8f5afc40f91c09f458"}, "ssvc": {"exploitation": null, "automatable": null, "technical_impact": null, "poc": false}, "barriers": {"attack_vector": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "summary": "Unknown"}, "weakness": {"cwe_ids": ["CWE-787"], "cwe_primary": "CWE-787", "cwe_family": null, "cwe_names": {"CWE-787": "Out-of-bounds Write"}}, "software": {"vendors": "FreeRDP", "products": "FreeRDP", "cpe_uris": "cpe:2.3:a:freerdp:freerdp:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*", "software_map": [{"key": "freerdp:freerdp", "vendor": "FreeRDP", "product": "FreeRDP", "source": "cna_vendor_product", "sample_cpe": null, "category": null, "platform": null, "surface": null, "tags": null}]}, "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/commit/5e8e987b469b60a3bafadf8f5afc40f91c09f458", "https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-m37j-jcr2-8gcc", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-before-heap-overflow-via-cliprdrstream-read"], "sources": {"vulners_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-68579", "nvd_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-68579"}}
{"id": "CVE-2026-67357", "identity": {"title": "CVE-2026-67357", "published": "2026-08-02 12:15:25", "modified": "2026-08-02 13:16:53", "description": "ArcadeDB versions before 26.7.3 contain an information disclosure vulnerability in the MCP get_server_settings tool that leaks the arcadedb.ha.clusterToken in cleartext. Attackers with MCP access can retrieve the cluster token and use it with X-ArcadeDB-Cluster-Token and X-ArcadeDB-Forwarded-User headers to impersonate root and achieve full server compromise."}, "cvss": {"base_score": 7.7, "severity": "HIGH", "attack_vector": null, "attack_complexity": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "scope": null, "confidentiality_impact": null, "integrity_impact": null, "availability_impact": null, "band": "High"}, "epss": {"score": null, "percentile": null, "date": null}, "exploitation": {"wild_exploited": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa_kev": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa": false, "has_exploit_bulletin": false, "has_exploit_reference": true, "has_public_exploit_provider": false, "has_github_exploit": false, "top_reference_url": "https://github.com/ArcadeData/arcadedb/security/advisories/GHSA-p9wc-4fhr-78wm"}, "ssvc": {"exploitation": null, "automatable": null, "technical_impact": null, "poc": false}, "barriers": {"attack_vector": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "summary": "Unknown"}, "weakness": {"cwe_ids": ["CWE-200"], "cwe_primary": "CWE-200", "cwe_family": null, "cwe_names": {"CWE-200": "Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor"}}, "software": {"vendors": "ArcadeData", "products": "arcadedb", "cpe_uris": "cpe:2.3:a:arcadedata:arcadedb:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*", "software_map": []}, "references": ["https://github.com/ArcadeData/arcadedb/security/advisories/GHSA-p9wc-4fhr-78wm", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/arcadedb-information-disclosure-via-get-server-settings"], "sources": {"vulners_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-67357", "nvd_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-67357"}}
{"id": "CVE-2026-68578", "identity": {"title": "CVE-2026-68578", "published": "2026-08-02 12:15:25", "modified": "2026-08-02 13:16:53", "description": "ArcadeDB versions before 26.7.3 fail to bind the authenticated principal in the MCP HTTP transport, causing all engine permission checks to silently pass as no-ops. Non-root MCP-allowed users can perform arbitrary database writes, DDL, schema mutations, and execute arbitrary JavaScript code via the query tool."}, "cvss": {"base_score": 7.7, "severity": "HIGH", "attack_vector": null, "attack_complexity": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "scope": null, "confidentiality_impact": null, "integrity_impact": null, "availability_impact": null, "band": "High"}, "epss": {"score": null, "percentile": null, "date": null}, "exploitation": {"wild_exploited": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa_kev": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa": false, "has_exploit_bulletin": false, "has_exploit_reference": true, "has_public_exploit_provider": false, "has_github_exploit": false, "top_reference_url": "https://github.com/ArcadeData/arcadedb/security/advisories/GHSA-6x73-v3rc-f57c"}, "ssvc": {"exploitation": null, "automatable": null, "technical_impact": null, "poc": false}, "barriers": {"attack_vector": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "summary": "Unknown"}, "weakness": {"cwe_ids": ["CWE-306"], "cwe_primary": "CWE-306", "cwe_family": null, "cwe_names": {"CWE-306": "Missing Authentication for Critical Function"}}, "software": {"vendors": "ArcadeData", "products": "arcadedb", "cpe_uris": "cpe:2.3:a:arcadedata:arcadedb:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*", "software_map": []}, "references": ["https://github.com/ArcadeData/arcadedb/security/advisories/GHSA-6x73-v3rc-f57c", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/arcadedb-authentication-bypass-via-mcp-transport"], "sources": {"vulners_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-68578", "nvd_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-68578"}}
{"id": "CVE-2026-67356", "identity": {"title": "CVE-2026-67356", "published": "2026-08-02 12:15:24", "modified": "2026-08-02 13:16:53", "description": "ArcadeDB before 26.7.3 binds the real LocalDatabase object into JavaScript trigger contexts with HostAccess.ALL, allowing schema-admins to call getSecurity().createUser() without permission checks. Attackers with UPDATE_SCHEMA permission can create triggers that execute JavaScript to create server-wide admin users, escalating privileges beyond their authorization level."}, "cvss": {"base_score": 8.8, "severity": "HIGH", "attack_vector": null, "attack_complexity": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "scope": null, "confidentiality_impact": null, "integrity_impact": null, "availability_impact": null, "band": "High"}, "epss": {"score": null, "percentile": null, "date": null}, "exploitation": {"wild_exploited": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa_kev": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa": false, "has_exploit_bulletin": false, "has_exploit_reference": true, "has_public_exploit_provider": false, "has_github_exploit": false, "top_reference_url": "https://github.com/ArcadeData/arcadedb/security/advisories/GHSA-38pf-6hp2-pxww"}, "ssvc": {"exploitation": null, "automatable": null, "technical_impact": null, "poc": false}, "barriers": {"attack_vector": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "summary": "Unknown"}, "weakness": {"cwe_ids": ["CWE-269"], "cwe_primary": "CWE-269", "cwe_family": null, "cwe_names": {"CWE-269": "Improper Privilege Management"}}, "software": {"vendors": "ArcadeData", "products": "arcadedb", "cpe_uris": "cpe:2.3:a:arcadedata:arcadedb:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*", "software_map": []}, "references": ["https://github.com/ArcadeData/arcadedb/security/advisories/GHSA-38pf-6hp2-pxww", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/arcadedb-before-privilege-escalation-via-javascript-trigger"], "sources": {"vulners_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-67356", "nvd_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2026-67356"}}
{"id": "CVE-2025-71401", "identity": {"title": "CVE-2025-71401", "published": "2026-08-02 12:15:23", "modified": "2026-08-02 13:16:52", "description": "better-auth (npm) before 1.4.2 allows an external request to configure baseURL when it is not otherwise defined (e.g., BETTER_AUTH_URL is unset). An attacker able to make the very first request to the server after startup can poison the router's base path, causing all routes to return 404 for all users (denial of service). The issue is not reachable when baseURL is explicitly configured or on typical managed hosting platforms."}, "cvss": {"base_score": 9.3, "severity": "CRITICAL", "attack_vector": null, "attack_complexity": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "scope": null, "confidentiality_impact": null, "integrity_impact": null, "availability_impact": null, "band": "Critical"}, "epss": {"score": null, "percentile": null, "date": null}, "exploitation": {"wild_exploited": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa_kev": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa": false, "has_exploit_bulletin": false, "has_exploit_reference": true, "has_public_exploit_provider": false, "has_github_exploit": false, "top_reference_url": "https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/security/advisories/GHSA-569q-mpph-wgww"}, "ssvc": {"exploitation": null, "automatable": null, "technical_impact": null, "poc": false}, "barriers": {"attack_vector": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "summary": "Unknown"}, "weakness": {"cwe_ids": ["CWE-770"], "cwe_primary": "CWE-770", "cwe_family": null, "cwe_names": {"CWE-770": "Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling"}}, "software": {"vendors": "better-auth", "products": "better-auth", "cpe_uris": "cpe:2.3:a:better-auth:better-auth:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*", "software_map": [{"key": "better-auth:better-auth", "vendor": "better-auth", "product": "better-auth", "source": "cna_vendor_product", "sample_cpe": null, "category": null, "platform": null, "surface": null, "tags": null}]}, "references": ["https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/security/advisories/GHSA-569q-mpph-wgww", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/better-auth-before-basepath-modification-dos"], "sources": {"vulners_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2025-71401", "nvd_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2025-71401"}}
{"id": "CVE-2025-71399", "identity": {"title": "CVE-2025-71399", "published": "2026-08-02 12:15:22", "modified": "2026-08-02 13:16:52", "description": "Better Auth relies on better-call, which uses the rou3 router library. In affected versions of rou3, paths are normalized by removing empty segments, so /path, //path, and ///path resolve to the same route. In Better Auth versions prior to 1.4.5 (which bundles the fixed rou3), this can allow attackers to bypass disabledPaths configuration and path-based rate limits by submitting requests with extra slashes in the URL path. The issue does not apply in deployments where the proxy or platform normalizes URLs by collapsing multiple slashes."}, "cvss": {"base_score": 8.8, "severity": "HIGH", "attack_vector": null, "attack_complexity": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "scope": null, "confidentiality_impact": null, "integrity_impact": null, "availability_impact": null, "band": "High"}, "epss": {"score": null, "percentile": null, "date": null}, "exploitation": {"wild_exploited": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa_kev": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa": false, "has_exploit_bulletin": false, "has_exploit_reference": true, "has_public_exploit_provider": false, "has_github_exploit": false, "top_reference_url": "https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/commit/f60b43fa648399534507c9ac7db36d705b8874c3"}, "ssvc": {"exploitation": null, "automatable": null, "technical_impact": null, "poc": false}, "barriers": {"attack_vector": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "summary": "Unknown"}, "weakness": {"cwe_ids": ["CWE-20"], "cwe_primary": "CWE-20", "cwe_family": null, "cwe_names": {"CWE-20": "Improper Input Validation"}}, "software": {"vendors": "better-auth", "products": "better-auth", "cpe_uris": "cpe:2.3:a:better-auth:better-auth:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*", "software_map": [{"key": "better-auth:better-auth", "vendor": "better-auth", "product": "better-auth", "source": "cna_vendor_product", "sample_cpe": null, "category": null, "platform": null, "surface": null, "tags": null}]}, "references": ["https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/commit/f60b43fa648399534507c9ac7db36d705b8874c3", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/better-auth-before-path-normalization-bypass-via-rou3", "https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/security/advisories/GHSA-x732-6j76-qmhm"], "sources": {"vulners_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2025-71399", "nvd_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2025-71399"}}
{"id": "CVE-2025-71400", "identity": {"title": "CVE-2025-71400", "published": "2026-08-02 12:15:22", "modified": "2026-08-02 13:16:52", "description": "better-auth passkey versions before 1.4.0 contain an insecure direct object reference vulnerability in the passkey deletion endpoint that allows authenticated users to delete arbitrary passkeys by ID. Attackers with valid sessions can submit crafted requests to the delete-passkey endpoint with enumerated passkey IDs to remove other users' passkeys."}, "cvss": {"base_score": 7.1, "severity": "HIGH", "attack_vector": null, "attack_complexity": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "scope": null, "confidentiality_impact": null, "integrity_impact": null, "availability_impact": null, "band": "High"}, "epss": {"score": null, "percentile": null, "date": null}, "exploitation": {"wild_exploited": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa_kev": false, "wild_exploited_by_cisa": false, "has_exploit_bulletin": false, "has_exploit_reference": true, "has_public_exploit_provider": false, "has_github_exploit": false, "top_reference_url": "https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/security/advisories/GHSA-4vcf-q4xf-f48m"}, "ssvc": {"exploitation": null, "automatable": null, "technical_impact": null, "poc": false}, "barriers": {"attack_vector": null, "privileges_required": null, "user_interaction": null, "summary": "Unknown"}, "weakness": {"cwe_ids": ["CWE-639"], "cwe_primary": "CWE-639", "cwe_family": null, "cwe_names": {"CWE-639": "Authorization Bypass Through User-Controlled Key"}}, "software": {"vendors": "better-auth", "products": "passkey", "cpe_uris": "cpe:2.3:a:better-auth:passkey:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*", "software_map": []}, "references": ["https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/better-auth-passkey-before-idor-via-delete-passkey", "https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/security/advisories/GHSA-4vcf-q4xf-f48m"], "sources": {"vulners_href": "https://web.nvd.nist.gov/view/vuln/detail?vulnId=CVE-2025-71400", "nvd_href": "